WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.129
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday. So ever since your brilliant video on Friday,

00:00:02.129 --> 00:00:04.460
I've been thinking about Florence Foster Jenkins.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:08.380
Her wikipedia article has perhaps the most damning first sentence I've ever read.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.840
"Florence Foster Jenkins was an American amateur operatic soprano,

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.560
who was known and ridiculed for

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.880
her lack of rhythm, pitch, tone, aburet pronunciation of libretti [?]

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.080
and overall poor singing ability."

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.180
But lest you think Wikipedia was exaggerating,

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.940
I'm gonna play you some Florence Foster Jenkins

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.500
while I show off how good I am at touching my toes.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:34.860
[Florence Foster Jenkins attempting to sing along whilst being accompanied by a piano]

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.600
Ah that was painful in more ways than one.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.440
So Hank, Florence Foster Jenkins began her singing career when she was 44 years old.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.999
She was divorced. Her parents had died.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.079
She'd inherited some money.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.200
And she decided to pursue her dream

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.140
of becoming a famous opera singer.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.240
And she had everything going for her;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.520
she had the drive, she had the time,

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.220
she had the money,

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.200
she wasn't afraid to fail.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.440
There was just the one problem

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.460
of being a terrible, terrible singer.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.489
And that's the crazy thing about Florence Foster Jenkins:

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:03.510
She couldn't sing at all,

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.860
but she really BELIEVED she could sing.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.460
She would come on stage, wearing wings

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.600
and sing Verdi and it would be like a total disaster,

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.120
except that she had fun

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.020
and everyone in the audience had fun.

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.620
So she had this fairly successful career

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:16.980
and then in 1944,

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:20.159
Florence Foster Jenkins finally made it to Carnegie Hall.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.940
She played a sold-out show at Carnegie Hall,

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:24.120
and she sucked.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.520
And this is vital, Hank,

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.480
because Florence Foster Jenkins set the bar for worst-ever Carnegie Hall performance

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.380
SO LOW,

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.460
that I believe we can jump over it.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.160
So, Hank, to celebrate the one-year anniversary of The Fault In Our Stars,

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.780
Penguin has rented out Carnegie Hall for us.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.089
And we're gonna have an evening of awesome, where we read and talk and play music.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:42.509
Don't worry,

00:01:42.509 --> 00:01:43.240
I won't sing.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.800
And all of my four favorite bands are going to be there

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.940
because of course my first favorite band is the Mountain Goats,

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.960
my second favorite band - also the Mountain goats,

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.820
my third favorite band is you, Hank,

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.940
and my fourth favorite band is the Mountain Goats

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.360
and the Mountain Goats are playing Carnegie Hall with us.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:57.119
It's gonna be awesome.

00:01:57.119 --> 00:02:00.560
We're gonna do our best to put on the greatest show that Carnegie Hall has ever seen.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.440
That's a lie,

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.769
we've got Richard Pryor to compete with, Andy Kaufman, Billie Holiday...

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.320
We are gonna be better than Florence Foster Jenkins.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.560
So Hank, as you saw earlier,

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.120
with my knees locked, I can't touch my toes.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:11.060
I can't even come close.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:12.360
As a result, realistically,

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.360
I'm probably never going to live my dream of being a professional contortionist.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.520
But Hank, as you well know,

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:17.720
I also can't sing

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:20.800
and I am going to live my dream of playing Carnegie Hall.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:24.380
Hank, obviously in life you have to find the places where your talents meet the world's needs.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.820
But the great lesson of Florence Foster Jenkins' life is that

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.370
aptitude is not destiny.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:33.120
I mean Hank, her voice sounded like the mating and/or death squeals of alley cats.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.440
But because she refused to be self-conscious about doing this thing that she sucked at,

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.789
people responded. They often responded by laughing,

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:39.880
but they responded.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:44.160
And it was obviously fulfilling for her because she sang for people professionally for like 40 years.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.000
It sucks not to be good at something you love

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.900
but I really admire people who do it anyway,

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.260
like I admire myself when I go to yoga class.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:53.080
And Hank, while I certainly hope we don't replace Florence Foster Jenkins

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:54.980
as the worst Carnegie hall performance of all time,

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.280
I admire her too.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:57.220
As she once put it Hank,

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.880
"People may say I can't sing

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:01.220
but no one can ever say I didn't sing."

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.140
[Singing] Some things you do for money,

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.800
and some you do for fun,

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.680
But the things you do for love,

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.820
are gonna come back to you

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.340
one by one.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:11.460
Hank,

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:12.860
I'll see you on Friday.

